on to the initial pressure. A particular type of pressure gain combustion (PGC) device is described, which is under investigation at GRC (Glenn Research Center). The Resonant Pulse Combustor (RPC) has been largely overlooked due to its theoretically low performance. However, its practical performance is quite competitive with other PGC systems, and its physical simplicity is unmatched.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","cui":{"isCui":false,"submissionId":20220014047,"id":"22fd3de7c0f94d7cb66148b0369f205c"},"meetings":[{"country":"US","submissionId":20220014047,"endDate":"2022-10-21T04:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"organizationId":"71fb4af96d4a59b5a0a2084db7b4ce35","meta":{"organization":{"name":"American Institute of Aeronautics and Astronautics","location":"Reston, Virginia, United States"}},"meetingId":"b72c75e355ac4157a285cd66195703a9","id":"274146bdfedb4016b772967f3af95fa5"}],"name":"AIAA Online Short Course: Fundamentals and Applications of Pressure Gain Combustion","location":"Virtual","id":"b72c75e355ac4157a285cd66195703a9","url":"https://www.aiaa.org/events-learning/courses-workshops/detail/fundamentals-and-applications-of-pressure-gain-combustion-online-short-course-(starts-sept-28-2022)","startDate":"2022-09-28T04:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"PGC Fundamentals 2022 RPC.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20220014047/downloads/PGC%20Fundamentals%202022%20RPC.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20220014047/downloads/PGC%20Fundamentals%202022%20RPC.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20220014047/downloads/PGC%20Fundamentals%202022%20RPC.pdf.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-10-08-04-13"}